      },
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Vincent is interested in war. Every weekend, he goes to the "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "firing range",
            "zh": "射击练习场"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " to shoot at “bad guys”. At home, he watches war films on repeat. He has read every war "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "memoir",
            "zh": "回忆录"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " he can find. Yet he has never been to a real war zone."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Here’s the question: Is Vincent missing something? Can real experience teach us what books or movies never can?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "These questions sit at the heart of "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "philosopher",
            "zh": "哲学家"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " Frank Jackson’s famous thought experiment: “What Mary Didn’t Know.”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "In the experiment, we meet Mary, a scientist who lives in a black-and-white world. But she isn’t alone. She has books and a computer. Mary learns everything about the colour “red”. She studies the science of light waves. She understands how the eye processes colour. She even knows the "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "symbolic",
            "zh": "象征性的"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " meanings of red, such as war and love. In short, Mary knows red inside and out."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Then, one day, Mary steps outside and sees a red rose for the first time. Does she learn anything new? Does seeing red add to her understanding of red?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "If the answer is yes, then we have to conclude that there’s more to life than the physical world. This was what Jackson had wanted to prove. But he later changed his mind. He argued that Mary didn’t actually learn anything new about the world. When she experiences red, nothing new pops up in the world. Her new understanding of red exists only in her mind, and she can describe it if she tries."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p7",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "And so the "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "debate",
            "ref": "v-debate"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " goes on. To me, there’s clearly a huge "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "divide",
            "ref": "v-divide"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " between how the world is described and how it is felt. Something special and unique happens when we experience something first-hand rather than just learn about it. Therefore, Vincent’s understanding of war can only go so far. If he ever experiences war himself, he’ll realise it could never possibly be "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "captured",
            "zh": "刻画"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " in a 90-minute film."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
